,4.507,[[0,0.898,341,153],[19,0.102,6,16]],[["",24,-1,1],["",24,-1,1],["",33,0,1],["",24,0,1]],0,1086],[7106377,20393,68,3.042,2.433,[[0,342]],[["",56,-1,1]],0,1087],[7103999,20396,506,10.07,8.247,[[0,0.986,343,719],[9,0.014,280,8]],[["",75,-4,1],["",75,-4,1],["",75,-4,1],["2b7d8394_528049b7",76,-1,1,"if?"]],0,1088],[6944413,20396,500,10.07,8.247,[[0,0.987,344,495],[25,0.013,1,6]],[["",77,-14,1],["",78,-14,1],["",79,-14,1],["",77,-14,1],["",80,-14,1],["",81,-4,1],["23e4dc78_b0f9ab69",81,0,1,"The absl::Hash() [documentation](https://abseil.io/docs/cpp/guides/hash) states this function should be added as a friend function. All the existing Chrome usage does that from what I see.…"]],0,1089],[7125799,20397,21,1.035,0.792,[[9,281]],[],0,1090],[7136214,20404,82,3.042,2.433,[[0,0.692,345,56],[24,0.308,96,26]],[],0,1091],[7136723,20405,23,1.035,0.792,[[0,346]],[["df6603ee_48fbd3b9",82,-1,0,"The `InstallErrorLogEntry` can also be used in the `ManifestToWebAppInstallInfoJob`, which can be run as part of manifest updating which is not an install command. For the future it might be nicer to…"]],0,1092],[7144278,20423,647,15.464,12.617,[[0,0.994,347,644],[9,0.006,282,3]],[["1623b13b_efaea715",82,-19,1,"nit: add space here?"],["1ed8924e_85e4da81",83,-19,0,"TIL about this, smart!"],["29126ac0_f2a3cd56",84,-19,1,"Let's make both of these constants?"],["2ac232b9_47890fc7",85,-19,1,"This is now carrying duplicate logs, because we're appending command logs to install manager logs here. Is this what you meant by the following? If so, can we add a `TODO(crbug.com/40224498): Unify…"],["2e4ca1ef_daa185fc",82,-19,1,"nit: `log_storage_for_disk_ `? `file_` could indicate that this is a `base::File` or something like that."],["318226f1_b6c8be25",84,-19,0,"nit: I found it easier to parse if `ReadLogFileBlocking()` is incorporated inside `PersistableLog`. It does seem like that function is not used anywhere else throughout this file, so adding it inside…"],["37dc0972_1ab2f23b",83,-19,1,"nit: It's easier to read `EXPECT_GT(CountRotatedLogs(command_manager_log_path), 0)` as there are more rotations than 0, but it's probably personal preference. Please feel free to disagree."],["4caeee35_de476114",83,-19,0,"Can we define this at the class level instead, so that we don't have to define this in every single test function?"],["4fb77c1e_362237f8",83,-19,1,"nit: It would be nice if we could expose a single `.log()` in both the `command_manager()` and `install_manager()` that could be used everywhere for readability."],["5878b8df_3a87c83c",84,-19,1,"Should this be renamed to `log_system_started_` or something like that? Judging by the name of the class `PersistableLog` and the name of this variable, I thought it meant that we were going to…"],["5dafc203_e01e8a3f",84,-19,1,"Why do we need to store both `log_storage_for_disk_` and `log_` separately? They're the same information once logs are being \"collected\", right? Or is there a different behavior, where `log_` only…"],["6a4b513b_2a3a4ce2",84,-19,0,"Hmmmm, this is an expensive I/O operation, because it rotates files by moving them if needed, AND then does a write. Since we do not perform `current_disk_log_file_.Resize()` anywhere, it seems like…"],["7fa50832_b626d881",32,-19,0,"This would be great. Having a single unified \"log\", such that we can just call `provider_->log()` or something like that to get access to the logs of the web_applications system would make things so…"],["82ed5ae8_c4dd25ac",83,-19,1,"Can we add comments here as to what is happening? Something like: ``` Flush the install manager and command manager so that all error logs are read from the disk and stored on memory if needed. ```"],["8bf99165_e2913728",84,-19,1,"Can you share why this is a `std::optional`? `rotated_filename` is always guaranteed to be created inside the `for loop`, even if there's one interation of the loop happening, so `rotated_filename`…"],["99c9c332_75abe32f",84,-19,1,"Let's make this a constant and then use it here? ``` static constexpr int kMaxIndexForFileRotation = 100; ```"],["9b159e4e_13e8f7c5",82,-19,1,"This doesn't exist yet, will `TakeCommandErrorLog()` be renamed or will this be a newly added function?"],["c3507c3d_13a502c3",83,-19,0,"Should this be defined at the class level instead for this test, since `FlushLogs()` is also technically a blocking operation, instead of doing it inside the scoped area here?"],["c6be8c0d_dcfa1cce",82,-19,1,"Is this comment correct? The comment says that this is a log, but is actually referring to an `int`. I would assume something like a `string` or a `base::Value` for a log, maybe this comment was for…"],["db9edd83_d24bb4df",84,-19,0,"I wonder if just adding `DLOG(ERROR)` here is enough. Imo, it isn't. If the point of these log files are for us to debug issues happening in Canary/Dev/Beta/Stable, then it's likely that these builds…"],["e1f25ffc_93922da3",84,-19,1,"Let's add comments to make this more readable, like for this one, we can add something like the following. We'll need to add one for `kEstimatedBytesPerLogEntry` as well. Also, where is this value…"],["f9ff54b7_bff0e74a",83,-19,1,"Let's add a comment: ``` // Ensure that the logs have persisted on disk by triggering log write // operations if needed. ```"],["fa92a1c5_062f2f56",82,-19,0,"Should we default initialize this to `0`, to prevent undefined behavior in case this is not constructed?"],["feb4c59a_ca447222",84,-19,1,"Aah, so we're only using the date string for file rotation? In that case, let's inline `base::UnlocalizedTimeFormatWithPattern(time, \"y-MM-dd\");` here?"],["352c7794_6beed024",86,-18,0,"Are the tests failing because the system is shutting down before `WebAppCommandManager::Start()` is called? Maybe we need to initialize the `log_` in the constructor instead, wdyt?"],["ab0ba4cc_a0a985de",84,0,1,"This function seems unused, let's remove?"],["b271736e_e783424e",87,0,0,"Hmmm why did we remove the `testing::StrictMock` here? This might cause future bugs to slip in as part of the `EXPECT_CALL` statements since we no longer verify which methods are interesting and…"],["d4804208_84d3df37",84,0,1,"We are using a global task runner `g_log_deletion_task_runner` here right? Can we remove this comment?"]],0,1093],[7209657,20424,361,10.07,8.247,[[0,0.997,348,361],[9,0.003,283,0]],[["8e72ff85_bd098f45",82,0,1,"nit: passing something by (const) reference that is expected to outlive the call is discouraged by the style guide since it can hide lifetime issues…"],["ad878b28_a79b218e",84,0,1,"nit: is this (and maybe other LOG(ERROR)s below left over debug code? If not, the message should probably be a bit clearer."]],0,1094],[7207934,20424,125,3.042,2.433,[[0,0.716,349,88],[9,0.284,284,37]],[],0,1095],[7233091,20427,9,0.597,0.431,[[0,350]],[],0,1096],[7264617,20439,101,3.042,2.433,[[0,0.748,351,75],[24,0.252,97,25]],[["0cae6bbd_503c1874",32,-1,0,"(not for this CL, but) should we consider making ManifestId a StrongAlias<GURL> rather than a GURL to try to catch mistakes like this? Not sure how annoying that would be to deal with..."],["1650e684_7c2ca4dd",88,-1,1,"huh, a comment on the gerrit IFTT design doc seems to imply that the // might be the problem, and that this should start with a single / instead."],["9888e78c_d4461948",32,-1,0,"is it a false trigger, or was it triggering because the IFTTT is not set up correctly? I would hope that IFTTT doesn't trigger for any newly setup instance..."],["b5b80c94_dd3dd26a",89,-1,1,"in the enums.xml file you specify a label for the IfChange in this file, but it's not here?"],["c0a99625_d511193e",89,-1,1,"this should include the :FetchManifestAndUpdateResult label I think?"],["e9be3ebe_3e9c6b50",71,-1,1,"nit: force"]],0,1097]]}